# Leftover renamed-not-deleted files — this sandbox's FUSE-mounted working
# tree supports rename() but not unlink(), so removing a tracked file goes
# through `mv <path> <path>.deleted` (same-directory rename, not a real
# delete) followed by `git add <path>` to stage the removal from git's
# perspective. The renamed leftover then just needs to stay out of `git
# status` noise — it can't be cleaned up from inside this sandbox either.
*.deleted

